# Static analysis for the myapi module (SPEC 124).
#
# What this adds that CI did not have. `php -l` proves a file PARSES, and the
# unit suite proves the lines it reaches BEHAVE — and on Drupal 7 there is a
# gap between the two that is wider than in most stacks. There is no autoloader
# and no imports: every call in this module is a bare global function name
# resolved at runtime, across 757 of our own functions in 60 files. A renamed
# helper whose old name survives in one caller, a typo in a function name, a
# variable spelled two ways in the same function — all of them parse, none of
# them is caught by a test that does not happen to walk that line, and each one
# is a white screen on the request that reaches it.
#
# Level 1 is what that gap costs to close: undefined functions, classes,
# constants and variables, plus wrong argument counts against our own
# signatures. It reports zero errors today, which is what makes it a gate
# rather than a report — the next one it prints is new.
#
# WHY NOT HIGHER. Level 2 currently reports 260, and 199 of them are one thing:
# SelectQuery and SelectQueryInterface, Drupal's query builder, which this
# module passes around and calls methods on. Clearing them means modelling
# core's database layer in tests/stubs/drupal7.stub.php, and that file's own
# rule is that it asserts names and never models behaviour — a stub that gets
# a signature wrong fails CI on correct code. The remaining 61 are all the same
# false positive too: PHPStan does not know that myapi_error() ends the request,
# so it reads `if (!$row) { myapi_error(...); }` as a branch that falls through
# and reports every dereference after it. Raising the level is a real piece of
# work with a real payoff; it is not a knob to turn on a whim.
#
# Both are run in CI on PHP 7.4 — phpVersion below pins the analysis to the
# version production runs, not the one the developer has.

parameters:
    level: 1
    phpVersion: 70433

    paths:
        - includes
        - resources
        - myapi.module
        - myapi.install

    # Drupal loads .inc/.module/.install as PHP; PHPStan has to be told.
    fileExtensions:
        - php
        - inc
        - module
        - install

    # Drupal core, which is not in this repository and never will be: the
    # module is deployed into a site that already has it. scanFiles (not
    # stubFiles, which registers no symbols) is what tells PHPStan these names
    # exist, so that the ones it still cannot find are ours.
    scanFiles:
        - tests/stubs/drupal7.stub.php
